   "verdict": "A failure indicates the Power Amplifier (A16) is probably at fault. Note what 'could not converge' means: the network's offset was so far out that the DAC ran out of range, which is a hard fault rather than a drift. U9 is a chopper-stabilised op amp precisely so that this offset stays tiny, so suspect U9, its 6.8 V supply zeners VR57 and VR58, and the switches U5 and K3 that set the input up.",
