   "noPublishedValue": true,
   "source": "Figure 7-19 sheet 1 legend (PG2D7); §5-22 step 11",
   "note": "Output of the sense-current cancellation circuit, and the signal routed to the Switch Matrix (A8) for the OUT/SENSE HI or SENSE HI binding posts. No level is published for TP1 on its own: §5-22 step 11 uses it as the reference for the one measurement that matters here, the 2 V ±25 mV between U1 pin 6 and TP1 at 100 V dc. Sense-current cancellation is active only in the dc 220 V range, so at any ac setting this node is doing nothing.",
